{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "00205",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 0.98,
      "end_seconds": 8.37,
      "duration_seconds": 7.39,
      "text": "Doctor, your next patient is here. I've done the basics, I'll read them out in a moment."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 9.91,
      "end_seconds": 13.47,
      "duration_seconds": 3.56,
      "text": "perfect, thanks. Hello there, so what's the trouble?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 14.55,
      "end_seconds": 17.27,
      "duration_seconds": 2.72,
      "text": "Doctor, thank you for seeing us."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 18.31,
      "end_seconds": 22.48,
      "duration_seconds": 4.17,
      "text": "Of course, please stay. It's helpful to have you here."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 23.27,
      "end_seconds": 26.27,
      "duration_seconds": 3.0,
      "text": "Well, I've been dealing with fever."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 27.86,
      "end_seconds": 30.41,
      "duration_seconds": 2.55,
      "text": "how long are we talking about?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 31.5,
      "end_seconds": 34.67,
      "duration_seconds": 3.17,
      "text": "I've had it for five days."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 35.48,
      "end_seconds": 44.54,
      "duration_seconds": 9.06,
      "text": "Tell me a bit more about it: how bad it gets, how often, and whether anything makes it better or worse."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 46.27,
      "end_seconds": 51.8,
      "duration_seconds": 5.53,
      "text": "I'd say severe. I get some relief from a cold sponge."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 53.35,
      "end_seconds": 56.77,
      "duration_seconds": 3.42,
      "text": "anything that tends to go along with it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 57.47,
      "end_seconds": 66.75,
      "duration_seconds": 9.28,
      "text": "A blocked nose goes along with it, most of the time. I've also had a sore throat"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 68.2,
      "end_seconds": 69.45,
      "duration_seconds": 1.25,
      "text": "how about rash?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 70.03,
      "end_seconds": 72.72,
      "duration_seconds": 2.69,
      "text": "Nope, uh, no rash."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 74.62,
      "end_seconds": 80.16,
      "duration_seconds": 5.54,
      "text": "actually, doctor, I did notice rash he doesn't always say"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 82.05,
      "end_seconds": 88.56,
      "duration_seconds": 6.51,
      "text": "No, I don't think I did. Maybe a little, I'm not sure."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 89.76,
      "end_seconds": 98.81,
      "duration_seconds": 9.05,
      "text": "alright, I'll note both what you've said and what you've noticed. And what about diarrhoea, chest pain or stiff neck?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 99.32,
      "end_seconds": 101.54,
      "duration_seconds": 2.22,
      "text": "nothing like that, no"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 101.81,
      "end_seconds": 105.59,
      "duration_seconds": 3.78,
      "text": "Mm. On the cardiac side, anything I should know?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 106.94,
      "end_seconds": 111.43,
      "duration_seconds": 4.49,
      "text": "hmm, uh, no, nothing with my heart"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 112.57,
      "end_seconds": 114.56,
      "duration_seconds": 1.99,
      "text": "so, how about exercise?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 120.92,
      "end_seconds": 124.62,
      "duration_seconds": 3.7,
      "text": "Not really, I don't get much exercise."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 126.43,
      "end_seconds": 128.7,
      "duration_seconds": 2.27,
      "text": "are you living with family?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 129.25,
      "end_seconds": 133.6,
      "duration_seconds": 4.35,
      "text": "I stay with my daughter and her family"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 135.19,
      "end_seconds": 138.85,
      "duration_seconds": 3.66,
      "text": "Tell me what you take day to day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 139.61,
      "end_seconds": 153.58,
      "duration_seconds": 13.97,
      "text": "Telmisartan, 40 milligrams, once a day. I just want to get back to to normal, really. I'd rather know what's going on than keep guessing."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 154.01,
      "end_seconds": 154.77,
      "duration_seconds": 0.76,
      "text": "Uh-huh."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 159.03,
      "end_seconds": 164.75,
      "duration_seconds": 5.72,
      "text": "Seretide inhaler. I take it twice a day. Paracetamol, when needed."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 166.85,
      "end_seconds": 169.23,
      "duration_seconds": 2.38,
      "text": "How much do you take?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 170.58,
      "end_seconds": 172.79,
      "duration_seconds": 2.21,
      "text": "It's, It's 500 milligrams."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 173.67,
      "end_seconds": 176.11,
      "duration_seconds": 2.44,
      "text": "Roughly how long on that one?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 177.74,
      "end_seconds": 179.92,
      "duration_seconds": 2.18,
      "text": "About nearly five years."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 189.19,
      "end_seconds": 199.12,
      "duration_seconds": 9.93,
      "text": "Do you have any allergies to medicines, food, anything at all? Bear with me, I'm just building up the the picture."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 200.97,
      "end_seconds": 204.55,
      "duration_seconds": 3.58,
      "text": "I don't have any known medication allergies."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 206.36,
      "end_seconds": 212.45,
      "duration_seconds": 6.09,
      "text": "I'm, I'm not sure that's right i seem to recall a problem with penicillin"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 214.02,
      "end_seconds": 217.22,
      "duration_seconds": 3.2,
      "text": "maybe, but I don't recall it"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 218.88,
      "end_seconds": 226.35,
      "duration_seconds": 7.47,
      "text": "Fair enough, I'll write down both versions. Any long-term health problems I should know about?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 227.19,
      "end_seconds": 230.01,
      "duration_seconds": 2.82,
      "text": "I've, I've got high blood pressure."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 231.14,
      "end_seconds": 231.84,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Understood."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 232.41,
      "end_seconds": 235.48,
      "duration_seconds": 3.07,
      "text": "I have asthma, for two years."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 237.44,
      "end_seconds": 245.42,
      "duration_seconds": 7.98,
      "text": "Right, so high blood pressure is already on your record. We'll keep that in mind today."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 260.76,
      "end_seconds": 263.24,
      "duration_seconds": 2.48,
      "text": "does anything run in the family?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 264.36,
      "end_seconds": 269.38,
      "duration_seconds": 5.02,
      "text": "my mother has diabetes my father had kidney stones"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 270.83,
      "end_seconds": 281.45,
      "duration_seconds": 10.62,
      "text": "Doctor, I've got the readings for you. Pressure 126 over 74, pulse is 99 beats a minute, SpO2 97 percent on room air, temp 38.5 degrees."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 283.43,
      "end_seconds": 284.13,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Thanks."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 286.16,
      "end_seconds": 289.57,
      "duration_seconds": 3.41,
      "text": "okay, I need to examine you for this"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 291.04,
      "end_seconds": 292.72,
      "duration_seconds": 1.68,
      "text": "Let me press here."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 304.73,
      "end_seconds": 311.03,
      "duration_seconds": 6.3,
      "text": "Your throat looks red at the the back, but there's no pus on the tonsils."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 311.84,
      "end_seconds": 315.64,
      "duration_seconds": 3.8,
      "text": "a little pressure here, tell me if it's tender"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 330.23,
      "end_seconds": 335.46,
      "duration_seconds": 5.23,
      "text": "The glands in your neck feel a little tender but not big."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0050",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 338.89,
      "end_seconds": 341.13,
      "duration_seconds": 2.24,
      "text": "okay, you can sit up"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0051",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 355.28,
      "end_seconds": 373.53,
      "duration_seconds": 18.25,
      "text": "Okay, thinking it through, my working impression is a viral upper respiratory infection. An early bacterial throat infection is still possible. Stop me if I've got anything wrong. You've had fever for five days, severe, and no stiff neck or diarrhoea."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0052",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 374.63,
      "end_seconds": 376.29,
      "duration_seconds": 1.66,
      "text": "that's it, yes"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0053",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 377.45,
      "end_seconds": 381.53,
      "duration_seconds": 4.08,
      "text": "we've already done a flu swab this morning, doctor"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0054",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 382.5,
      "end_seconds": 388.67,
      "duration_seconds": 6.17,
      "text": "Thanks, I'll look at that. Blood tests is what I'd like next, for fever."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0055",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 390.29,
      "end_seconds": 392.11,
      "duration_seconds": 1.82,
      "text": "Is that done here?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0056",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 393.65,
      "end_seconds": 421.98,
      "duration_seconds": 28.33,
      "text": "I think a throat swab makes sense here, for sore throat. I'd like you to take cetirizine, 10 milligrams, at night, for five days. It's for blocked nose. Stay home, rest, and keep the fluids up. Warm soups and water, anything that goes down easily. One warning sign to remember: the symptoms get worse. In that case don't wait. Book a review in five days. Right, that's all. Go gently."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0057",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 423.79,
      "end_seconds": 429.75,
      "duration_seconds": 5.96,
      "text": "right, uh, no, I think that's everything. Thank you, doctor"
    }
  ]
}